{"book":24,"chapter":3,"context":{"chapter":3,"title":"Return, Faithless Children","summary":"Using the picture of an unfaithful wife, God compares Israel, the northern kingdom already in exile, with her 'treacherous sister' Judah, who learned nothing. Yet He calls both to return, promising shepherds after His own heart and a day when Jerusalem will be called the Lord's throne.","background":"The Law forbade a man to take back a divorced wife who had married another (Deuteronomy 24:1-4), which makes God's 'return again to me' (v. 1) astonishing. The northern kingdom had fallen to Assyria in 722 BC, about a century earlier. This message comes from Josiah's reign (v. 6), when Judah's reform may have been only skin-deep, 'feignedly' (v. 10).","customs":[{"term":"The ark of the covenant","verses":"3:16","note":"The gold-covered chest in the temple's inner room, symbol of God's throne. Its fate is unknown; it is never mentioned again after Jerusalem's fall."}],"watchFor":["'Return' is repeated again and again (vv. 1, 7, 12, 14, 22).","Verse 22 plays on one Hebrew root: 'backsliding' children and healing their 'backslidings.'","The chapter ends with the people's confession (vv. 22–25)."],"connections":["Deuteronomy 24:1-4","2 Kings 17:5-6","Hosea 14:1-4","Ezekiel 23:2-4"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["לֵאמֹר","lemor","H559","HR/Vqcc","<to> saying"],["הֵן","hen","H2005","HTj","there!"],["יְשַׁלַּח","yeshalach","H7971","HVpi3ms","he will send away"],["אִישׁ","'ish","H376","HNcmsa","a husband"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["אִשְׁתּוֹ","'ishto","H802","HNcfsc/Sp3ms","wife his"],["וְהָלְכָה","vehalekhah","H1980","Hc/Vqq3fs","and she will go"],["מֵאִתּוֹ","me'ito","H854","HR/Rd/Sp3ms","from with <the> him"],["וְהָיְתָה","vehayetah","H1961","Hc/Vqq3fs","and she will belong"],["לְאִישׁ","le'ish-","H376","HR/Ncmsa","to a man"],["אַחֵר","'acher","H312","HAamsa","another"],["הֲיָשׁוּב","hayashuv","H7725","HTi/Vqi3ms","¿ will he return"],["אֵלֶיהָ","'eleiha","H413","HRd/Sp3fs","to 